&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Associated with United Chinese Basketball Association&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Designed and developed AI-driven technologies supporting athlete evaluation, basketball analytics, and community engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developed BERT- and deep learning-based models for player ranking using scouting reports, game statistics, and media evaluations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built computer vision pipelines for basketball action recognition and real-time performance analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designed a basketball community platform integrating player engagement, court discovery, and event management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="player-development-in-practice"&gt;Player Development in Practice&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alongside analytics development, I observe and document high-level youth basketball training to connect technical models with real coaching environments. Sessions with the New York Rens AAU program—which featured Don Bosco Prep guard
, the No. 2 overall player in the 2024 high school class—inform my understanding of player development, practice design, and the on-court context behind performance data.&lt;/p&gt;
